ol registration definition object lacks an input parameter schema field.", "The LLM client failed to complete the initial JSON-RPC handshake.", "The workspace environment variable path contains invalid escape characters."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "Every MCP tool definition must contain an inputSchema object declaring expected arguments. Missing this property violates the MCP specification, causing static analysis tools to flag a schema validation warning."}, "notes": "Let me check your understanding of schema validation errors.", "los": ["CO1.LO2"], "sources": [], "minutes": 5}, {"kind": "concept", "title": "Integration Testing Strategies for Custom Tools", "bullets": ["Public integration test suites simulate agent clients by sending protocol JSON payloads.", "Tests assert tool availability, parameter validation, and response structures.", "Mocking stdio streams enables automated pipeline testing without running full agent hosts.", "Passing all public integration tests confirms complete protocol compliance."], "figure": {"kind": "none", "caption": "", "steps": [], "code": "", "language": "", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "Testing your MCP custom integration requires more than basic unit tests. Public integration tests simulate real host-client JSON-RPC messages over stdio or HTTP streams, verifying that your server responds according to specification.", "los": ["CO1.LO2"], "sources": [], "minutes": 6}, {"kind": "worked_problem", "title": "Executing Integration Tests Against Tool Servers", "bullets": ["Step 1: Instantiate mock test client connected to local MCP server process.", "Step 2: Issue tools/list request and assert tool presence in output array.", "Step 3: Dispatch tools/call with sample parameters and assert response content.", "Step 4: Verify test suite reports 100% pass rate with zero static warnings."], "figure": {"kind": "code", "caption": "Python Integration Test Implementation", "steps": [], "code": "def test_linter_tool_execution(mcp_test_client):
    response = mcp_test_client.call_tool(
        "run_static_analysis",
