uring test execution.", "The client protocol transport header specifies an unsupported character encoding."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'Invalid params' is a standard JSON-RPC protocol error indicating that runtime parameters supplied in tools/call failed schema validation (e.g., passing a string for an integer field)."}, "notes": "Consider this troubleshooting scenario from a common test failure.", "los": ["CO1.LO2"], "sources": [], "minutes": 5}, {"kind": "summary", "title": "Summary: Custom MCP Tool Integration Best Practices", "bullets": ["MCP standardizes communication between AI agents and developer tool suites.", "Define complete JSON Schemas with explicit parameter types and descriptions.", "Validate workspace configurations with static analysis tools to remove warnings.", "Verify tool integrations using automated public integration test suites."], "figure": {"kind": "none", "caption": "", "steps": [], "code": "", "language": "", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "To wrap up: Model Context Protocols provide a clean standard for extending AI workspace capabilities. Always write explicit schemas, validate configurations statically to avoid warnings, and cover tool endpoints with integration tests. Thank you for your attention!", "los": ["CO1.LO2"], "sources": ["C1"], "minutes": 5}]}

