 updates status'", "Missing primary trigger", "Carrier sends status update callback"]]}, "quiz": null, "notes": "When converting requirements into executable specs, watch out for vague claims. AI coding assistants fail or hallucinate when specifications contain ambiguous terms. Clarifying boundaries and metrics ensures both human developers and AI agents produce correct code.", "los": ["CO2.LO3"], "sources": [], "minutes": 6}, {"kind": "activity", "title": "Hands-On Exercise: Outlining System Use Cases", "bullets": ["Task: Read the provided product blurb for a smart warehouse service.", "Step 1: List all primary actors and secondary external integrations (e.g., Carrier, System Administrator).", "Step 2: Draft one short use case in YAML format including pre/postconditions.", "Step 3: Peer review to confirm no internal system elements are misclassified as actors."], "figure": {"kind": "flow", "caption": "Activity Workflow", "steps": ["Read Short Description", "Identify External Actors", "Draft YAML Use Case", "Validate Boundaries"]}, "quiz": null, "notes": "Now it's time for an in-class hands-on exercise. Take 10 minutes to work through the provided warehouse management product blurb. Identify the external actors—remembering never to list the system itself as an actor—and write down a structured YAML use case.", "los": ["CO2.LO3"], "sources": [], "minutes": 10}, {"kind": "summary", "title": "Summary: Custom Tools and Requirements Specs", "bullets": ["Model Context Protocol enables standardized, warning-free integration of tools into AI workspaces.", "Typed parameters and clean schemas prevent runtime errors during agent tool calls.", "System boundaries isolate internal application logic from external actors (users and external APIs).", "Standardized use case specs provide clear, executable guidelines for software development."], "figure": {"kind": "none"}, "quiz": null, "notes": "To summarize today's lecture: MCP gives us a clean, standard protocol for extending agent capabilities with custom tools. Meanwhile, standard use case guidelines help us translate unstructured requirements into clear system boundaries with external actors like carriers and system administrators. In the upcoming lab, you will build and test custom MCP tools hands-on!", "los": ["CO1.LO2", "CO2.LO3"], "sources": ["C1"], "minutes": 4}]}

